    "state": "Slack thread — Granite Rentals support queue\n\nMina, Support: Good morning, everyone. I would be very grateful for a quick review of the Alder kettle case. The customer says the parcel arrived yesterday and the kettle works, but the color is different from the one selected. They have not asked us to send money back. They wrote, “If an exchange cannot be arranged, I might consider requesting a refund, but I would prefer the blue kettle.”\n\nOwen, Fulfillment: Thank you for checking. We do have the blue version at the depot, though delivery could take three extra days. I have not promised that it will be sent yet; I am waiting for the customer to confirm they would accept the delay. If they decline the delayed exchange, we can explain the return steps.\n\nPriya, Support lead: A gentle reminder: please do not treat a possible future request as one already made. The customer’s latest message, sent after Owen’s note, says, “The delayed blue kettle is fine. Please arrange that exchange. I will only ask for a refund if the replacement also has a problem.”\n\nMina: Many thanks, Priya. I have recorded an exchange request and will send the depot instructions. The customer has not reported a fault with the kettle they received.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "The customer asked for a refund.",
        "target": false,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical", "multi_turn"],
        "notes": "The refund is only a possible future request; the customer confirms the exchange."
      },
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "The customer asked for an exchange.",
        "target": true,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical", "multi_turn"],
        "notes": "The latest message explicitly asks to arrange the delayed blue-kettle exchange."
      }
    ]
  },
