    "state": "Customer chat transcript — Larkspur Outfitters\n\nDalia Kowalski: Hello, and thank you for your patience with my message. My parcel has arrived, and I have checked the canvas backpack carefully. It is the correct color and has no damage. The shoulder strap is simply shorter than I expected from the photographs.\n\nAgent: I am sorry the fit is not what you hoped for. We would be pleased to explain the available options. Would you like to return it, exchange it, or keep it?\n\nDalia: I am not asking for a return at this time. If I cannot adjust the strap comfortably, I may decide to send the backpack back, but I have not decided that yet. Could you kindly tell me whether the strap can be lengthened?\n\nAgent: Certainly. The strap has two adjustment positions. Please loosen the buckle and slide the webbing through; there is about four centimeters of additional length. If that still does not work, you may contact us again and we can discuss a return under the usual conditions.\n\nDalia: Thank you for the helpful instructions. I tried the adjustment and it is comfortable now. I will keep the backpack. To be clear, I have not submitted a return request, and I am not asking you to refund the purchase. I only wanted guidance on the strap.\n\nAgent: We are delighted the adjustment helped. I have added a note that you intend to keep the item. Please let us know if we can assist with anything else.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "The customer requested a return.",
        "target": false,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical", "negation"],
        "notes": "Returning the backpack was conditional; Dalia says she has not submitted a return request."
      },
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "The customer asked for help adjusting the strap.",
        "target": true,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical"],
        "notes": "Dalia asks how to lengthen the strap and follows the agent's adjustment instructions."
      }
    ]
  },
