    "state": "Terms of Service excerpt provided in a Copperleaf Studio support conversation\n\nReturns and exchanges. We are pleased to help customers find a suitable resolution. A customer may request a return within 21 calendar days after delivery, provided the item is unused and all original packaging is present. A request made after that period is not eligible for a standard return. This timing rule is based on the delivery date, not the order date.\n\nPossible future requests. A customer’s statement that they might return an item, would return it if a problem occurred, or may request a refund after considering another option does not itself constitute a return or refund request. Support staff should record a request only when the customer actually asks us to initiate that remedy. A question about how a remedy works is not an instruction to initiate it.\n\nReplacement exception. If an item is confirmed defective within 45 calendar days after delivery, the customer may request a replacement even when the 21-day standard return period has passed. This exception authorizes a replacement only; it does not extend the standard return period and does not automatically authorize a refund. A defect must be reported as an existing condition, rather than described solely as something that could happen in the future.\n\nIllustration: A customer who says, “If the zipper breaks, I would like a replacement,” has not yet reported a defect or asked for an immediate replacement. A customer who says, “The zipper has broken; please send a replacement,” has reported a present defect and made an actual request. Please apply these provisions courteously and avoid treating possibilities as completed requests.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "A customer who says they might return an item has made a return request.",
        "target": false,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical", "negation"],
        "notes": "The excerpt explicitly says a possible future return does not constitute a request."
      },
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "A customer with a present defect reported within 45 days may request a replacement after the 21-day return period.",
        "target": true,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical", "exception"],
        "notes": "The 45-day defect exception permits a replacement after day 21, but not a refund."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "state": "Customer chat transcript — Northwind Health\n\nDmitri Rahman: Good afternoon, and thank you for looking into this so kindly. I ordered a compact heated eye mask from your shop. It arrived this morning in good condition, and it is the model I selected. I have not tried it yet because I am waiting for the instruction leaflet to arrive separately.\n\nAgent: Thank you for explaining. I am very sorry the leaflet was not in the parcel. I can email a copy if that would be useful. Are you asking us to cancel the order or refund the payment?\n\nDmitri: No, please do not cancel anything. If the leaflet shows that the mask is unsuitable for me, I might ask to return it later. At present I would simply appreciate the leaflet. I have not decided that the product is unsuitable, and I have not asked for money back.\n\nAgent: Of course. I have emailed the leaflet to the address on the order. For completeness, the instruction sheet says not to use the mask if its heating surface is damaged. Have you found any damage?\n\nDmitri: I have not found damage. I was only asking about the leaflet, not reporting a defect. I will read it before deciding whether to use the mask. If I discover a problem after that, I can contact you, but there is no problem I can report now.\n\nAgent: Many thanks for clarifying, and I am pleased to have sent the requested information. Your order remains active, and we have not opened a return or refund case.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "The customer reported that the eye mask is damaged.",
        "target": false,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical", "negation"],
        "notes": "Dmitri explicitly says no damage has been found; a future problem is only conditional."
      },
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "The customer asked the company to email the instruction leaflet.",
        "target": true,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical"],
        "notes": "Dmitri asks for the leaflet now; possible later return or refund is not requested."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "state": "Teams thread — Larkspur Outfitters order follow-up\n\nElena, Customer Care: A very pleasant afternoon to you both. I am reviewing Tomasz Lindqvist’s order for a ceramic travel mug. He says the mug arrived intact, but he accidentally selected the smaller size. In his first message he wrote, “If the larger size is still available, could you tell me how an exchange would work?” He did not ask us to start an exchange in that message.\n\nRavi, Orders: Thank you, Elena. The larger size is available. I sent the customer the exchange instructions and clarified that we can proceed once he confirms. I have not changed the order or created a return label.\n\nElena: I appreciate the careful distinction. His reply just came in: “Thank you for explaining. Please do not start an exchange yet. I would like to keep the mug I received, but if it feels too small after I use it for a week, I may contact you to ask about exchanging it.”\n\nRavi: Understood with thanks. That is a possible later request, not an instruction to initiate an exchange now. The mug has not been used, according to the customer, and no defect is alleged. Our size exchange route remains available if he contacts us with an actual request, subject to the policy details already sent.\n\nElena: Much obliged. I will close the follow-up as an information inquiry only. To avoid any confusion, the customer has neither asked for a refund nor asked us to send the larger mug. He has received the instructions and says he will decide after trying the item.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "The customer asked the company to start an exchange.",
        "target": false,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical", "multi_turn"],
        "notes": "He asks how an exchange works, then expressly says not to start one; later exchange is conditional."
      },
      {
        "type": "binary",
        "instruction": "The customer asked for a refund.",
        "target": false,
        "hard_cases": ["hypothetical", "negation"],
        "notes": "The thread explicitly states he has not asked for a refund."
      }
    ]
  }
]

