    "state": "Community handbook: player conduct and account requests\n\nWelcome to the Lantern Vale gaming community. This page explains the ordinary rules for members who play together, use the discussion boards, or ask moderators for help. The rules apply in public rooms and private community matches when the match is hosted through our service. Please read the whole page before opening a support ticket. Our moderation team works in several time zones, so a clear request with the relevant match date is easier to handle than several short messages.\n\nRespectful play is expected. You may disagree about a map, a strategy, or a team decision, but do not insult another player or repeatedly send unwanted messages. A first minor issue normally receives a reminder. Serious threats, account theft, or repeated harassment can lead to a temporary or permanent account restriction. Moderators review the actual report and available chat record; a player cannot decide another player's punishment by posting a demand in chat. Reports should identify the account and explain what happened. Please do not publish private addresses or payment details in a report.\n\nTrade and account safety are also important. The community does not arrange sales of accounts, and members should never share passwords. If you believe your account was accessed by somebody else, use the account-recovery form. A moderator can explain the next steps but will not ask you to send a password in a message. Game items obtained through ordinary play are not exchanged for cash by community moderators. Any outside offer is the responsibility of the members involved and is not a community-supported transaction.\n\nFor purchases made through the Lantern Vale store, a player may request a refund within fourteen calendar days after the purchase if the purchased content has not been used. The request must be sent through the store form and include the order reference. Used content is not eligible under this ordinary rule, even if the request is made within fourteen days. This rule applies to store purchases, not to gifts bought by another player. If a purchase is missing from an account, contact support first; a missing item report is not itself a refund request. Support will check the order record before deciding whether a refund can be issued.\n\nMatch suspensions can be appealed once through the appeal form. Explain why you think the restriction was applied incorrectly and include the match code if you have it. An appeal does not automatically remove the restriction while the review is happening. Posting the same appeal repeatedly does not make the review faster. Moderators do not promise a particular outcome, but they aim to send a decision after checking the available record.\n\nThe community calendar lists scheduled maintenance and friendly events. A cancelled event is not a punishment, and a delay to maintenance does not mean a player's account is affected. Members can mute event announcements without leaving the community. For technical problems, include the device type and a short description of what you saw. Do not post a long list of unrelated complaints in a ticket; separate issues help support answer each one clearly. These guidelines may be updated when the store or game changes, and the date shown at the top of the page identifies the current version.",
