    "state": "Player review: Mosslight Headset\n\nI bought the Mosslight Headset from the Copperleaf Supply community shop because my old headset gave a sharp noise whenever I joined a party. I play mostly cooperative quests and sometimes sit in the community voice room while other players discuss map routes. The order arrived in a plain paper box with a small folded instruction sheet. Nothing in the packaging looked fancy, but the headset itself was protected well and was easy to take out without pulling on the cable.\n\nMy first test was on a quiet evening. The ear pads felt soft and did not press too hard around my glasses. After two hours, the headset was still comfortable, although my ears were warm. The microphone arm moves smoothly and stays where I put it. My friends said my voice was clear, and they did not hear the background fan that used to be obvious with my previous headset. The mute switch is easy to find by touch. It makes a small click, which is useful because I can tell when I have switched it off without looking away from the game.\n\nThe sound is good for party chat and game effects. Footsteps and door sounds are easy to notice, and the voice channel does not become harsh when several people speak at the same time. Music has enough detail for normal play, but players who want powerful bass for listening to music may prefer another model. I used the headset on a desktop and on a handheld game device. Both worked without a special program. On the handheld device, the cable was a little long, so I tied it loosely rather than letting it reach across the desk.\n\nThere are two small problems. The control wheel is close to the cable connection, and I turned it by accident a few times when moving the headset. Also, the included instruction sheet does not explain the mute light very clearly. I eventually learned that the light is visible only from the side. These are not major issues, but the store page could give a better picture of the controls. The cable connection stayed firm during my tests, and I did not hear the crackling sound that made me replace my old headset.\n\nI used it on six evenings over about two weeks. It worked each time, and the microphone did not suddenly become quiet. I did not test it in a tournament or in a very loud room, so I cannot say how it performs in those conditions. I also have not tested the headset with a console that needs a separate adapter. My comments are only about the devices I listed. The shop packed the order carefully, and the delivery arrived on the date shown in the order page.\n\nOverall, I would recommend this headset to community members who need comfortable voice chat and clear game sounds without extra software. It is not the strongest choice for music listeners who want heavy bass, and the control wheel placement takes some getting used to. For my cooperative games, it solved the voice clarity problem and stayed comfortable for ordinary sessions. I would keep it rather than return it. I am giving this review after actual use, not after reading the store description alone.",
    "questions": [
      {
