    "state": "Lantern Vale community page: events and shared rooms\n\nThis page explains how the community schedules friendly game events and uses shared rooms. It is written for players who want to join without needing to know a moderator personally. Event notices appear on the calendar page and in the community announcement channel. Each notice gives the planned start time, the game mode, and the maximum number of places. When an event is full, members may still ask to be placed on a waiting list, but a place is not guaranteed until the event host confirms it.\n\nFriendly events are not ranked competitions. Players should follow the mode instructions given by the host and allow others to take a turn when the event format requires it. A host may pause an event if the room has a technical problem or if a player needs help understanding the rules. Pausing does not mean that the event has been cancelled. If the host does cancel an event, the calendar entry will be marked cancelled and a new date may be posted later. Members should check that entry instead of assuming that an old chat message is the latest schedule.\n\nShared rooms are open voice and text spaces for people who want to find a group. Please use the room connected to the game mode you are playing. A room host can move a discussion to another channel if it is unrelated to the game. Players may mute a room or leave it at any time. Leaving a room does not remove a player from the community, and muting does not block that player from joining a game later. Moderators may remove messages that contain private contact details, password requests, or unwanted personal attacks.\n\nA player who cannot attend an event should use the event page's leave button when possible. That allows the host to offer the place to someone on the waiting list. It is helpful to leave a short note, but it is not required. Sending a message that says “maybe I can come” does not reserve a place. If a member asks the host to save a place and the host confirms it, that confirmation is the information to rely on. The page does not treat an unconfirmed request as a reservation.\n\nFor event problems, contact the host first if the host is available. If the problem concerns harassment, account access, or a purchase, use the support form so that it reaches the right team. Do not post a password or a payment number in the event chat. The community cannot restore a lost account just because a member mentions the issue during a friendly match. Support will ask for the details needed through the secure form and will tell the member what steps are available.\n\nThe event calendar is maintained by volunteers, and the listed times use the time zone shown beside each event. Members should check that zone before planning a session. A past event may remain visible for several days as a record of what took place, but its date does not mean that the event is still open. New players are welcome to read the room rules and join an event that has available places. We ask everyone to be patient with volunteer hosts and to give clear information when requesting help. This page describes the normal community process and does not promise that every event will run exactly on schedule.",
