    "state": "Incident postmortem: weekly map room audio problem\n\nIncident summary\nOn 7 June, players using the weekly map room could hear game sound but could not hear other people speaking through the room's voice channel. Text chat remained available. The problem affected the weekly map room only. Other community voice rooms continued to work during the same period. This report is for members who want to know what failed and which actions were taken. The operations team has written the sequence in ordinary language because the internal monitoring terms are not useful to most players.\n\nWhat players noticed\nThe first message said that two party members could see each other's names in the room but did not hear speech. Several people then tested their own headsets and reported similar results. Some players could still hear music and game effects through their devices, so those sounds were not evidence that the room voice channel was working. A few members initially thought the issue was caused by their microphone settings. The team checked the room service before asking anyone to change device settings. No player had to reinstall the game or replace a headset to resolve the service issue.\n\nTimeline\nAt 18:42, the room monitoring page recorded a rise in failed voice connections for the weekly map room. At 18:47, a moderator forwarded the first player report to the operations group. At 18:55, the team confirmed that text messages were still arriving and that other voice rooms were operating normally. At 19:06, operations compared the room settings with the settings for a working room and found that the weekly map room was pointing to an outdated voice channel address. The channel address had been changed during a routine room setup earlier in the day, but the weekly map room entry had not been updated.\n\nAt 19:15, the team corrected the address and restarted the room connection. A small test group joined and confirmed that they could hear one another. At 19:22, the operations team checked again with a second group, including a player who had first reported the issue. That group also confirmed that speech was working. The incident was marked resolved at 19:30. The time between the first monitoring alert and resolution was 48 minutes. The problem did not affect saved match records, purchases, account sign-in, or the game sound effects heard locally by players.\n\nCause and response\nThe outdated address directed voice connections to a channel that was no longer active. Because the room could still carry text messages through a separate service, members could type normally even while voice connections failed. The team corrected the room entry rather than changing player accounts or asking members to reset their devices. Reports of a missing game item that appeared in the same discussion were checked separately and did not share this cause. The team did not find evidence that a player's microphone or headset caused the room-wide failure.\n\nFollow-up work\nWe have added the weekly map room to a check that compares its voice channel address with the current room list. The check will run after routine room setup changes. The room host will also receive a short notice if the voice connection check fails, while text chat remains available. This should make it easier to distinguish a room service issue from an individual device problem. Operations will verify the new check during the next scheduled room update. Until that test is complete, moderators will continue to use the existing monitoring page and respond to reports from players.\n\nWe apologize to members who planned a voice session and found that they could not speak with their group. Thank you to the players who supplied clear reports and remained in text chat while the team tested the correction. A report about a whole room is especially useful when it says which room is affected and whether text chat still works. Members who continue to experience an individual audio problem after the room is confirmed working should then check their own device settings or contact support.",
