r reporting a sync fault; Granite Software is the vendor investigating it. I am repeating this because the case form’s autogenerated summary currently says “vendor requests customer refund,” which is an impressive inversion even by ticketing standards.\n\nFrom: Oren Vale\nTuesday, 11:12\nThe queue now shows the archive chunk was accepted, then the worker lost its lease. We restarted the worker. We will send a written incident summary and confirm whether the credit provision applies after we calculate the actual service interruption. We are not asking Granite Studio for a refund.\n\nFrom: Nadiya Pell\nTuesday, 11:27\nThanks. Please send the summary to our workspace administrators. We are asking for an explanation of the interruption and restoration of the project. We are not offering a credit to your company, and we are not requesting payment from your supplier. If a service credit is due under your terms, that is your accounting decision to communicate to us.\n\nCase footer, auto-generated, Tuesday 11:31: reporter=Nadiya Pell / Granite Studio; responder=Oren Vale / Granite Software; issue=archive sync; requested_action=investigate, restore, explain; refund_claim=none; finance forward=excluded. Footer authorship is the ticket system’s, and should not be confused with who sent the original messages. The mail archive also includes an old subject-line match, “refund process,” which refers to a different tenant and is not attached to this thread.",
