    "state": "Incident postmortem: Harbor Studio annual development-credit reconciliation\nPrepared by Farid Kowalski, People Operations\n\nOn 3 September, the internal review desk received a question about whether an employee's annual development-credit record should be sent to the central learning administration queue. The rule for this program is based on the total confirmed variance between the credit award authorized for the year and the amount posted for that same year. When the variance is at least 12 credits, the case goes to central learning administration. A variance below 12 credits is resolved by the department's HR contact. Credit amounts from separate employees or separate years cannot be combined.\n\nThe employee's signed authorization lists an annual award of 48 credits. The system record lists 35 credits posted for the same annual cycle. A separate note lists 2 credits as scheduled for a course next month, but those credits have not been posted and are not included in the current system balance. The reconciliation worksheet also contains a 1-credit entry from the prior annual cycle. That entry is displayed beside the current total because the export covers two cycles; it is not part of this year's authorized award or posted amount. The original reviewer added the scheduled 2 credits and prior-cycle 1 credit to the posted total before calculating a provisional variance.\n\nThe policy owner reviewed the signed authorization and confirmed that the comparison must use only the current cycle's authorized and posted figures. The scheduled course entry remains prospective until completion and posting. The prior-cycle entry remains attached to its original year. There is no evidence that either record was transferred into the current cycle. The employee asked the HR contact for clarification, but no correction request has been filed and no one has asserted that the authorization itself is wrong.\n\nThe incident was caused by the export's adjacent-cycle layout, which did not visually separate prospective items from posted credits. The export will be revised to present a separate annual-cycle subtotal and a distinct column for scheduled activity. Reviewers have been instructed to verify the period labels before routing. This report addresses destination only; central administration, if engaged, would verify the underlying entries and would not automatically grant additional credits. The employee's course schedule, department budget, and prior-year total are included in the source file for context but do not change the current-year variance calculation.",
