ssed inspection, excluding the date of the original appointment. The next business day is Friday, 21 June; there is no holiday exception in this offer. If the technician attends by 15:00 Friday, the fee-credit condition does not arise. This offer does not say a later portal closeout is required by 15:00; attendance at the site is the relevant event.\n\n08:51 — Technician: I have now read the full access note. I left at 13:18, before the cycle ended. I cannot honestly say the customer prevented access for the full slot. My draft closeout saying “relay passed, sensor replaced” is also wrong: no relay test was done, and no sensor was replaced. A relay pass cannot be inferred from the green dispatch icon. The icon only means the route was assigned.\n\n09:06 — Crew lead: There is a safety exception, but it is narrow. If the cabinet remains energized and a qualified person documents a specific hazard, the relay test may be postponed with supervisor approval. No such hazard report exists for Thursday. The active misting cycle is a reason to wait until 13:25, not a reason to omit all tests. The replacement threshold is separate: a sensor reading at or below 80 means no replacement is required, even if the customer is angry about the visit.\n\nFriday, 21 June, 14:42 — Technician: Returned at 14:35, after the greenhouse confirmed the cycle was off. Sensor reading was 78 again; did not replace, as required. Tested backup relay: it failed to switch during the prescribed check. I did not complete the moisture sensor’s second confirmation because the meter probe was damaged. I reported that defect to the supervisor; the work order requires a safe, functioning meter before the confirmation. The supervisor has not approved an exception to omit it.\n\n14:49 — Kwame: I am glad somebody finally tested the relay. I am not saying the whole job is fixed. The probe problem is yours, not a refusal from me. Since your technician attended before 15:00, I am not asking for the fee credit under the missed-visit offer. Keep the ticket open for the sensor confirmation, and stop marking it complete just because the relay failed loudly.",
