    "state": "FAQ excerpt copied from the North Quay Learning Centre course-admin page. It has clearly been edited by several people, because some answers are tidy and some sound like someone explaining things over a cup of tea.\n\nQuestion: Where do I see my enrolled courses?\nAnswer: Sign into the learner portal and open “My Learning.” The office can help if a course that you already enrolled in does not appear. A course merely viewed in the catalogue will not appear there, which is a small distinction but a useful one.\n\nQuestion: Can I change sections after enrolling?\nAnswer: You can ask the course office to check whether another section has space. A request is not a completed transfer, and staff should confirm the new section before you plan around it. If the course page is being updated, the portal may take a little time to catch up.\n\nQuestion: What if I cannot attend the first meeting?\nAnswer: Write to the instructor or course office and explain the situation. They can tell you what material is available. The FAQ does not promise that every class is recorded, and it does not say that missing a meeting automatically changes your registration.\n\nQuestion: How do I get an accessible copy of a handout?\nAnswer: Tell the office which document you need and what format works for you. Staff can arrange an accessible version or point you to an existing one. You do not need to explain personal medical details in the initial request.\n\nQuestion: Does the centre offer refunds?\nAnswer: Refund eligibility depends on the course and the timing of a withdrawal. Ask the office to check the rule that applies to your enrolment. This page describes how to ask for information; it does not confirm that any particular learner has requested a refund or qualifies for one. Please do not assume a withdrawal request and a refund request are identical.\n\nQuestion: Can I borrow a tablet?\nAnswer: Some classes have shared equipment, but availability varies. The course page or instructor should say whether equipment is supplied for that class. If you do not see an answer, contact the office and we can find out. We would rather check than tell you to bring something you may not need.\n\nQuestion: Where are the readings?\nAnswer: Instructors may put readings in the portal, distribute them in class, or provide a list of library materials. If you cannot locate a specific reading, send its title to the office. Please do not assume the reading is missing simply because it is not on the first page you opened.\n\nQuestion: Can the office change my mark?\nAnswer: The office can forward an administrative query to the instructor, but instructors decide academic marks. If you believe a mark was entered incorrectly, say which course and item you mean. A general question about grading policy is not itself a request to change an individual mark.\n\nStaff note: This FAQ is meant to describe processes, not to fill in facts about individual students. If you are reading a student’s message alongside this page, keep the two sources separate. The FAQ may explain that refund questions can be sent to the office, for instance, but that does not show that a particular student sent one. Same for section changes: being allowed to ask is not the same as having asked. The centre has been trying to avoid recording assumptions in the enrolment file, because assumptions are annoying to unwind later.\n\nAnother note from the web editor: “The equipment answer is deliberately cautious. We had one class where tablets were supplied and another where students used their own, so we should not turn that into a general promise. If a person asks whether equipment is available, record that question. Don’t silently transform it into a request to borrow a particular device.”",
