    "state": "Forwarded email. Cover note from the service coordinator: Sending this whole thread along because Wanjiru Moreau’s notes are much clearer than my calendar entry, and I don’t want anyone guessing which part was actually replaced. The attachments are summarized below because the original photos are in the job folder.\n\nForwarded message\nFrom: Wanjiru Moreau, field technician\nTo: repair desk, Larkspur Labs\nSubject: Tuesday visit — greenhouse control panel\n\nHi all,\n\nI went over to the greenhouse office this morning for the control panel visit. The site manager had said the screen was hard to read in bright light, and also that the arrow buttons sometimes seemed slow. I first wiped the screen with the approved cloth and checked the brightness setting. The screen was readable after that, including with the office blinds open. I pressed each arrow button several times and they all responded at once; I couldn’t find a sticking button or a delay. I didn’t replace the screen and I didn’t change the panel configuration.\n\nThe separate humidity sensor was also on the bench beside the panel. It had a cracked outer cover, so I replaced the cover with the spare listed on the work order. The sensor readings continued to display normally before and after. That was the only physical part I replaced today. I left the old cover in the labeled returns bag, not in the general waste bin, because the desk asked us to keep damaged covers for the quarterly count.\n\nThe manager showed me a small paper note saying the panel had “gone dark” last week. We checked the event history together. That message was from a brief power interruption, not a screen failure, and it cleared when power returned. The manager said the panel has been running since then. I recorded the historical event as context, not as an open fault. We tested the screen again after cleaning and it stayed readable. The manager signed the service slip and asked me to email the summary to the shared site mailbox.\n\nNo one asked for a refund, discount, or reversal of an earlier service charge. The visit was covered by the normal maintenance arrangement, and there was no discussion of a disputed invoice. The manager did ask whether we could leave a spare cloth in the office for next time, so I gave them one from the van stock and wrote that down as a no-charge consumable. I did not promise a new panel or a new sensor. The panel remains installed, the buttons responded during my test, and the humidity sensor is still installed with its replacement cover.\n\nFor the closeout, please list the screen as cleaned and tested, arrow buttons as tested with no fault found, and sensor cover as replaced. The screen itself was not replaced. The panel event from last week should stay in the notes as a resolved power interruption rather than a repair item. I’m heading to the depot now and can answer questions after lunch.\n\nThanks,\nWanjiru\n\nAttachment summary: service slip signed by greenhouse manager; one spare cleaning cloth issued; one cracked humidity-sensor cover returned; no other parts recorded. The coordinator has checked the forwarded thread against the work order and says the visit is ready to close.",
