    "state": "Northwind Supply\nPeople Operations — spreadsheet extract pasted from the annual training tracker\nReporting period: January to March\nPrepared for internal review by Bao Petrov\n\nThe following rows were copied from the tracker as text. Status labels reflect the decision field at the time of export. A blank cell is not a negative decision; it means no value was entered. The training rule shown in the header applies to the completion column: an employee is complete only if the required modules are marked complete. The rule does not say that an unmarked module should be treated as completed.\n\nColumns: employee | required modules | completed modules | attestation | manager note | review status\n\nRow 41 | Employee A | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | submitted | “All required modules recorded; no outstanding item noted.” | complete\n\nRow 42 | Employee B | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | Respectful Workplace; Safety Basics | submitted | “Records Handling not yet recorded. Employee says they have not failed to take it; completion is awaiting the learning portal sync.” | pending\n\nRow 43 | Employee C | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling | submitted | “Safety Basics is not marked incomplete in the manager’s note, but the module field is blank. Do not infer completion from the absence of a failure flag.” | pending\n\nRow 44 | Employee D | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | blank | “Modules all appear complete. No attestation has been submitted, so the row is not complete under the annual rule.” | pending\n\nRow 45 | Employee E | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | Respectful Workplace; Safety Basics | submitted | “Employee reports taking Records Handling last week, but there is no completion record yet. The supervisor has not confirmed a sync.” | pending\n\nRow 46 | Employee F | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | Respectful Workplace; Records Handling; Safety Basics | submitted | “No module is outstanding. Attestation received.” | complete\n\nThe annual rule, reproduced above the original tracker, reads: “Completion requires all three named modules to be recorded as complete and the employee attestation to be submitted. A status of pending is not complete. Do not infer that a blank or unconfirmed entry is complete merely because the employee says the course was taken. Do not treat a missing failure flag as positive evidence.” A separate instruction says managers may correct a verified portal sync error, but may not change the requirement or substitute an informal message for the completion record.\n\nReview note, 2 April: The report is intended to identify rows requiring follow-up, not to determine whether employees attended a live session outside the portal. Bao Petrov checked the displayed values against the export and confirmed that the labels were preserved exactly. The spreadsheet contains no additional completion evidence beyond the module and attestation fields shown. In particular, a submitted attestation does not fill in a missing module record, and complete module records do not replace a missing attestation.\n\nThe operations team considered whether to count rows marked “not incomplete” as complete. It rejected that approach: the phrase can indicate only that a reviewer did not enter a failure label. The actual tracker status and the required fields govern. Likewise, a note saying that a person has “not failed to take” a course is not a completion entry. If a sync issue is confirmed later, a corrected export may be issued with an audit trail; no such correction is included here.\n\nFor the present extract, the review question is limited to recorded completion under the stated annual rule. It does not assess effort, attendance, eligibility for an exception, or whether a person intends to finish later. Rows 42, 43, and 45 have at least one required module without a complete record. Row 44 has all module records but lacks the required attestation. Rows 41 and 46 meet both recorded requirements. These descriptions are supplied as context for interpreting the tracker, not as permission to change its fields.",
