    "state": "Meridian Software — school course administration invoice and accompanying account record\nPrepared for the fictional Northbank Learning Centre, 14 September 2025\nAccount contact: Tomasz Petrov, course administrator\nInvoice number: MS-8041\nService period: September 2025\n\nThis invoice covers the centre’s use of Meridian Software’s course administration platform. It is an ordinary monthly account document, prepared from the quantities recorded in the centre portal on 10 September. The school uses the platform to organize course descriptions, class rosters, room requests, and instructor access. The invoice does not include tuition collected from students, textbook purchases, or payments to instructors. Those items are handled by the school and are not part of this supplier account.\n\nLine items\n1. Course administration platform, one monthly school subscription: $480.00\n2. Instructor portal access, 12 active instructor accounts at $15.00 each: $180.00\n3. Student roster import, one completed import service: $65.00\n4. Additional roster import, quantity 0 at $65.00 each: $0.00\n5. Classroom scheduling add-on, one monthly add-on: $90.00\n6. Printed course catalogues, quantity 0 at $8.00 each: $0.00\n7. Account setup fee: $0.00, waived under the school’s existing account arrangement\n\nSubtotal: $815.00\nTax: $0.00\nTotal due: $815.00\nPayment due: 30 September 2025\n\nThe quantities above are the billed quantities, not estimates for the following month. The 12 instructor accounts were active during the September service period. The school may remove accounts before the next billing cycle by using the account page. Removal after the period begins does not alter this invoice. There is one completed roster import listed. The additional-import line is present on the standard invoice form but has a zero quantity and zero charge. No catalogue printing was ordered for this period.\n\nPayment record and account notes\nA payment of $815.00 was received on 16 September 2025. The payment was posted to invoice MS-8041 on the same day, and the account balance for this invoice is now $0.00. The payment was made by the school office using the saved institutional payment method. A separate payment of $90.00 dated 2 September belongs to invoice MS-7990 for the prior service period; it is not a second payment against this invoice. The accounting page displays older invoices below the current entry, so a reader should use the invoice number to distinguish them.\n\nAccount contact note, 10 September: “Please keep the classroom scheduling add-on for September. We are using it for room assignments. We are not asking to cancel the subscription.” This message is recorded for account context and does not change the September invoice. The note refers to keeping the add-on active, not to an additional charge beyond the single listed monthly add-on. The school’s request to keep the service is not a refund request.\n\nAdministration checklist completed by the supplier\n- The current invoice number was matched to the September service period.\n- The billed instructor count was checked against the portal snapshot.\n- The roster import count was checked against the service log.\n- Zero-quantity standard lines were left visible so the school could see that they were not billed.\n- The total was checked against the accounting system before issue.\n- The payment was matched by invoice number after it arrived.\n\nThe supplier account page sometimes shows a general balance summary as well as individual invoices. The general balance summary can include unpaid amounts from other billing periods, but the individual entry for MS-8041 remains the authority for this invoice. At the time this record was exported, the account had no unpaid balance for MS-8041. This does not make a claim about a different invoice that may be displayed elsewhere in the account history.\n\nSupport record\nA short support message from the school asked whether the “extra import