    "state": "Northbank Learning Centre course office — customer chat transcript and case summary\nChat date: 6 October 2025\nService provider: Harbor Studio\nSchool contact: Esi Bergstrom, evening course coordinator\nCase reference: HC-2196\n\nThe following transcript was saved by the school’s course office after a discussion about a short evening class. It includes the original question, the provider’s replies, and a staff summary. The class is called Introductory Clay Forms and is scheduled as a six-session course in the centre’s ceramics room. The chat concerns the course booking and the school’s administrative record. It does not concern a student complaint about instruction or a request to change a grade.\n\n09:12 — Esi: Hello. I am checking the booking for Introductory Clay Forms. The course page says six sessions, Wednesdays, 6:00 to 7:30. Is that still correct?\n09:14 — Harbor Studio support: Hello Esi. Yes, the booking currently shows six Wednesday sessions, from 6:00 to 7:30 in the ceramics room. The first meeting is 15 October.\n09:16 — Esi: Good. I need to check what was included in our course administration payment. Did we pay for printed handouts or only room use and the instructor booking?\n09:18 — Harbor Studio support: The school booking includes the room and instructor reservation. Printed handouts are not included in that booking. They can be requested separately, but we do not see a handout order on this case.\n09:20 — Esi: Please add ten printed handout packs, one for each enrolled student. The office will send the final student count if it changes.\n09:22 — Harbor Studio support: I have added a request for ten handout packs to case HC-2196. The current request is ten packs. The price will be confirmed in the separate supply quotation before printing.\n09:24 — Esi: Thank you. Please do not change the six class dates. I am not asking to cancel or reschedule the course. I only want the handouts request recorded.\n09:25 — Harbor Studio support: Understood. The six class dates remain as booked. The handout request is recorded separately and does not alter the course schedule.\n\nThe transcript has been included in the school file because staff wanted a clear record of what was requested. The school’s first question was about the contents of the existing booking. Support answered that room use and instructor reservation were included, while printed handouts were not included. Esi then made a separate request to add ten printed packs. The request is not evidence that the packs were already included in the original booking. It is a new request that will require a separate quotation before printing.\n\nCourse record at the time of the chat\nCourse title: Introductory Clay Forms\nMeetings: six\nDay: Wednesday\nTime: 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.\nRoom: ceramics room\nFirst meeting: 15 October 2025\nStatus: booked\nInstructor reservation: confirmed\nRoom reservation: confirmed\nHandout order: requested, quotation pending\nCancellation request: none\nRescheduling request: none\n\nThe course office entered the requested handout quantity as ten because that was the number supplied by Esi in the chat. The student count may later change, but no revised number appears in this transcript. The office has not yet approved a price for the packs. Harbor Studio has not printed or delivered them. The booking record therefore distinguishes between the confirmed course arrangements and the pending supply request.\n\nA previous case shown in the support system concerns a different class. It was a Saturday watercolor workshop that used eight easels. The note says that the workshop organizer asked for six extra brushes. That case does not relate to Introductory Clay Forms, and its quantities should not be copied into this record. The ceramics course has no stated easel or brush order. The other case is displayed in the system because the same school account used Harbor Studio for more than one activity.\n\nSchool office follow-up, 7 October\nThe course administrator reviewed the transcript and confirmed that the current task is to obtain a quotation for ten handout packs. The administrator did not authorize printing before the school sees the price. The office checklist marks the room booking as confirmed and the instructor reservation as confirmed. It marks handout printing as “waiting for quotation.” It leaves the schedule unchanged. No refund, cancellation, or rescheduling work is opened.\n\nHarbor Studio’s standard school booking process is recorded below for clarity. First, the school identifies the course and its dates. Second, the provider confirms room and instructor availability. Third, additional materials can be requested. A request for materials is not treated as an accepted purchase order until the quotation is approved. Fourth, the provider prepares the materials after approval. In this case the course booking has passed the first two stages. The handout request has been entered but has not passed the quotation-approval stage.\n\nThe transcript does not say that all students have paid tuition. Tuition collection is handled by the school and is not a Harbor Studio service. It also does not say that the school asked for more class meetings. The stated course remains six meetings. The phrase “one for each enrolled student” explains why ten packs were requested; it does not establish that ten people attended a class or that ten packs have already been produced.\n\nCase notes entered by support\n- Contact: Esi Bergstrom, evening course coordinator.\n- Main question: whether handouts were part of the current booking.\n- Answer: no; room and instructor reservation are part of it, printed handouts are separate.\n- New request: ten printed handout packs.\n- Price: awaiting separate quotation.\n- Schedule: unchanged, six Wednesday meetings.\n- Case status: open for quotation follow-up.\n\nThis file is a chat record rather than a final invoice. It contains no amount paid for handouts and no evidence of a refund. The provider has recorded the requested quantity and will send the quotation. Until that quotation is approved, the school should not treat the requested packs as delivered materials. The original booking remains active for its six listed meetings. The chat is retained so a substitute course-office worker can answer questions consistently without confusing the materials request with the confirmed room and instructor arrangements.",
