    "state": "Course services agreement excerpt, amendment record, and school filing note\nParties: Harbor Studio and Westmere Evening School\nSchool contact: Priya Delgado, programme secretary\nAgreement file: HS-WE-33\nEffective date of original clause: 1 January 2025\n\nOriginal clause 7 — course materials and room administration\nHarbor Studio will reserve the agreed classroom and instructor for each course listed in an approved booking form. The school may request printed course materials as an additional service. Printed materials are not included in the room reservation or instructor reservation unless an approved booking form expressly lists them. The price and quantity for any printed materials must be recorded in writing before production begins. A request made by email or chat allows Harbor Studio to prepare a quotation, but it does not by itself authorize printing. The school’s programme secretary or another named school approver must accept the quotation in writing before Harbor Studio begins production.\n\nFor a course booking, the school is responsible for providing the final course title, meeting dates, expected room capacity, and any approved materials order. Harbor Studio is responsible for reserving the room and instructor according to the accepted booking form. A later change to the dates or materials must be recorded in an amendment or a revised booking form. No staff member should infer a change only because another course at the school uses a different schedule or a different materials quantity.\n\nThe agreement distinguishes between an inquiry, a request, and an accepted order. An inquiry asks what is available or what an item costs. A request asks the provider to consider supplying an item. An accepted order requires written approval of the quotation. The provider’s acknowledgment that a request has been recorded is not the same as acceptance of a price, production, or delivery date. These distinctions apply to the course services in this file.\n\nAmendment 1, dated 12 February 2025\nThe parties agree that a school may cancel a confirmed classroom reservation without an administration charge if written notice is received at least 14 calendar days before the first scheduled meeting. Notice received fewer than 14 calendar days before that meeting does not meet the free-cancellation condition. The notice date is the date the provider receives the school’s written message, not the date the school drafts or saves it. This amendment changes only the cancellation condition. It does not include printed materials in a room booking and does not remove the written-approval requirement for materials orders.\n\nAmendment 2, dated 3 April 2025\nThe school may name a programme secretary to send booking messages and request quotations. The named secretary may not approve an additional charge unless the school has also recorded that person as an authorized purchaser. Priya Delgado is named as programme secretary for Westmere Evening School. The authorized purchaser list in the file names the school bursar and the head of programmes. It does not name the programme secretary. The amendment gives Priya permission to request information and quotations, but it does not give her authority to approve charges on the school’s behalf.\n\nBooking form for “Reading Skills for Tutors”\nAccepted on 5 August 2025\nFirst meeting: 1 October 2025\nMeetings: four Tuesdays\nRoom: Seminar Room B\nInstructor: confirmed\nMaterials section: no printed materials listed\nThe booking form was accepted by both parties. It is the operative record for the course dates, room, instructor, and materials listed at that time. No separate materials quotation is attached to this form.\n\nEmail record, 8 September 2025\nPriya to Harbor Studio: “Could you tell me the price to print twelve reading packets for our October tutor course? I am checking whether the school can add them. Please send a quotation before any printing.”\nHarbor Studio to Priya: “We will prepare a quotation for twelve packets. No printing will begin before written approval by an authorized purchaser.”\nThe email is filed as a quotation request. It does not record an accepted price or an order approval. No quotation response or approval is attached to this agreement excerpt.\n\nEmail record, 10 September 2025\nPriya to Harbor Studio: “Thank you. Please keep the room and instructor booking as confirmed. I am not approving a packet charge yet. I will ask the bursar to review any quotation.”\nThis message preserves the existing booking and explicitly says that Priya is not approving a packet charge. It does not cancel the course, change its dates, or authorize production of packets. The school’s request for a quotation remains separate from its accepted course booking.\n\nAmendment register review, 15 September 2025\nThe school filing clerk checked the document list. Amendment 1 is signed by both parties. Amendment 2 is signed by both parties. No later amendment changes the materials clause, the named secretary’s authority, or the cancellation notice rule. A draft note in the folder suggests that “the secretary can approve all course expenses,” but the note is marked unapproved and has no signatures. It is not an amendment and does not replace the authorized purchaser list.\n\nAdministrative guide attached to the contract file\nA confirmed booking should be checked against the accepted booking form. A possible extra service should be checked against a quotation and the authorized purchaser record. A cancellation should be checked against the first meeting date and the date notice was received. Staff should not treat a request for information as a purchase, or a draft document as an agreed change. The agreement is intended to make the responsibilities clear for school staff and provider staff who may not have taken part in the original conversation.\n\nCourse office checklist\n- Correct course title matched to booking form: yes.\n- First meeting date matched: yes, 1 October 2025.\n- Room reservation: confirmed.\n- Instructor reservation: confirmed.\n- Printed packets on accepted form: no.\n- Quotation requested: yes, for twelve packets.\n- Quotation approved by authorized purchaser: no record found.\n- Priya Delgado listed as authorized purchaser: no.\n- Course cancellation notice received: none.\n\nThis excerpt is provided for school administration training. It contains no student names, grades, attendance records, or tuition information. The agreement concerns services between the school and Harbor Studio. A packet request should not be recorded as a completed materials purchase unless the required approval is later found. Likewise, a statement that the booking should remain confirmed is not a cancellation. The signed documents and the attached emails are included together so that staff can identify which statements are operative and which are only requests or drafts.",
